      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. INTRODUCTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Coal and petroleum are exhaustible natural resources formed from prehistoric organic matter over millions of years.",
        "Carbonisation is the slow chemical process by which dead vegetation turns into coal under high pressure and temperature.",
        "Petroleum refining yields crucial fuels and products including petrol, diesel, kerosene, LPG, and bitumen.",
        "Combustion of fossil fuels releases harmful gases such as CO2, SO2, and NOx, causing air pollution and global warming."
      ],
      "id": "4ohehbu"
    },
